# Upstream: zyedidia/micro (MIT). See NOTICE.md.
# Lossy on purpose: note's lexer keeps word lists and
# delimiters, not micro's regular expressions.

name = Zsh
extensions = zsh
quotes = "'
keywords = always break bye case continue disown do done elif else esac exit fi for function if in local read return select shift then time until while bindkey builtin cd declare eval exec export jobs let popd pushd set source typeset umask unset find kill killall make pkill sed tar base64 basename cat chcon chgrp chmod chown chroot cksum comm cp csplit cut date dd df dir dircolors dirname du echo env expand expr factor false fmt fold head hostid id install join link ln logname ls md5sum mkdir mkfifo mknod mktemp mv nice nl nohup nproc numfmt od paste pathchk pinky pr printenv printf ptx pwd readlink realpath rm rmdir runcon seq shred shuf sleep sort split stat stdbuf stty sum sync tac tail tee test timeout touch tr true truncate tsort tty uname unexpand uniq unlink users vdir wc who whoami yes
